{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803814-belial-s-brood-and-the-strix","id":803814,"title":"Belial's Brood and the Strix","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-08T09:54:00-08:00","id":803814,"title":"Belial's Brood and the Strix","content":"Hi everybody and happy new year,<br /> <br /> To make a long story short, I started my Chronicle as a VtR one, when Blood and Smoke hit the shelves I was thrilled and decided to go from Requiem to Blood and Smoke but, instead of putting the Strix into the Background, stating that they've always being there, I turned Blood and Smoke into a Chronicle during which, eventually, the Strix will raise again after being gone for centuries and forgotten by most kindred. So here I am, reworking my whole Chronicle, and using a Belial's Brood covey as a nemesis, they are plotting to summon a demon (possibly Belial himself) through a terrible ritual. Eventually they will fail because they were fooled by the Strix: the centuries old book they're using as a blueprint to conduct the ritual is a fake, a clever scheme weaved by the Strix itself a long time ago: the ritual won't summon a demon but open a portal to Dis and allow the Strix to plague our world again.<br /> <br /> I took notes on all this and read the Belial's Brood sourcebook again and it rose some questions:<br /> <br /> 1) The Nameless are actually talking about Dis and that didn't catch my attention at first when I read the sourcebook but now I'm thinking &quot;Great ! Right on the money!&quot; but wait, according to the Nameless' myths it's not an underworld place but a very earthly place, a long time ago even before Babylon blossomed. Do you think Blood and Smoke is talking about is the same Dis the Belial's Brood sourcebook is referring to ? <br /> 2) My first idea was: the Forsworn were fooled and will perish at the end of the ritual, being the ultimate sacrifice for the Strix to return. I loved the idea: you're playing with fire and now you're being consumed by it because they are forces that even a badass vampire cannot hope to harness. But, thinking about it, how would the Strix react to the Belial's Brood philosophy ? It seems to me, they are quite similar, it seems to me that Blood and Smoke turned the Belial's Brood into the Strix. What do you think ? And if the Strix and the Forsworn ain't the same concept what would be the difference and how they see each other ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:33:18-08:00","id":803834,"title":"","content":"As per #1, the place Strix come from isn't named in 2e. It's just &quot;the empty shadow-place&quot; in the Shadow Potency 10 manifestation that opens a gateway there.<br /> <br /> I assume &quot;Birds of Dis&quot; to be a poetic name given to them by Vampires. Dis is the name of the lowest regions of Hell in Dante's Inferno. They're hell-birds. I don't think they actually come from a plane called Dis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:42:15-08:00","id":803841,"title":"","content":"To be honest, it looks like Belial's Brood might be a heretical branch of the Lancea et Sanctum in 2e. Look at the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZXnaJDf-gERGZe97JoIqj2bffJyrjal8Ch4xWD4L9lg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Pledge to the Worthless One</a> Miracle.<br /> <br /> As for the difference... well, what makes you think that Belial <i>isn't</i> a Strix? I think it adds a bit more to the irony if the ritual isn't fake - it's just that they misunderstood who they're summoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:43:56-08:00","id":803843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803814-belial-s-brood-and-the-strix?p=803841#post803841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, it looks like Belial's Brood might be a heretical branch of the Lancea et Sanctum in 2e. Look at the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZXnaJDf-gERGZe97JoIqj2bffJyrjal8Ch4xWD4L9lg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Pledge to the Worthless One</a> Miracle.<br /> <br /> As for the difference... well, what makes you think that Belial <i>isn't</i> a Strix? I think it adds a bit more to the irony if the ritual isn't fake - it's just that they misunderstood who they're summoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a feeling they will keep the idea of BB having mutliple groups. Heretical Sanctified might just only be one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:50:37-08:00","id":803846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803814-belial-s-brood-and-the-strix#post803814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everybody and happy new year,1) The Nameless are actually talking about Dis and that didn't catch my attention at first when I read the sourcebook but now I'm thinking &quot;Great ! Right on the money!&quot; but wait, according to the Nameless' myths it's not an underworld place but a very earthly place, a long time ago even before Babylon blossomed. Do you think Blood and Smoke is talking about is the same Dis the Belial's Brood sourcebook is referring to ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would certainly be an interesting story hook to follow, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) My first idea was: the Forsworn were fooled and will perish at the end of the ritual, being the ultimate sacrifice for the Strix to return. I loved the idea: you're playing with fire and now you're being consumed by it because they are forces that even a badass vampire cannot hope to harness. But, thinking about it, how would the Strix react to the Belial's Brood philosophy ? It seems to me, they are quite similar, it seems to me that Blood and Smoke turned the Belial's Brood into the Strix. What do you think ? And if the Strix and the Forsworn ain't the same concept what would be the difference and how they see each other ? </div> </div> </div>The Belial's Brood still exists, and were more introspective than outwardly-aggressive like the strix. But it is possible that they are sort of seen with approval by the strix, as they are about losing their Humanity. Whether they're losing their Humanity to become strix or sticking with their original goals would probably be up to you. If you want to go by the books, though, traditionally the Brood serve the Inferno, while the strix are something else. Still, it wouldn't be far-fetched to have the Brood be a sort of birthplace for new stirges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:06:37-08:00","id":803857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803814-belial-s-brood-and-the-strix?p=803834#post803834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per #1, the place Strix come from isn't named in 2e. It's just &amp;quot;the empty shadow-place&amp;quot; in the Shadow Potency 10 manifestation that opens a gateway there.<br /> <br /> I assume &amp;quot;Birds of Dis&amp;quot; to be a poetic name given to them by Vampires. Dis is the name of the lowest regions of Hell in Dante's Inferno. They're hell-birds. I don't think they actually come from a plane called Dis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep I took it quite literally because I had no intel about where they came from but this hint, could be a poetic expression, point taken <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:14:34-08:00","id":803862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803814-belial-s-brood-and-the-strix?p=803841#post803841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, it looks like Belial's Brood might be a heretical branch of the Lancea et Sanctum in 2e. Look at the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZXnaJDf-gERGZe97JoIqj2bffJyrjal8Ch4xWD4L9lg/edit#&amp;quot;]Pledge</a> to the Worthless One[/URL] Miracle.<br /> <br /> As for the difference... well, what makes you think that Belial <i>isn't</i> a Strix? I think it adds a bit more to the irony if the ritual isn't fake - it's just that they misunderstood who they're summoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true but anyone could receive the Call.<br /> You got me ^^, I didn't phrased my question like this but, deep down, I was wondering &quot;are the the Forsworn and the Strix on the same team ? Do I have to choose and pick the one who's going to fill that role in my Chronicle ? And if I do pick both, what kind of different niches are they going to serve ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:31:00-08:00","id":803873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803814-belial-s-brood-and-the-strix?p=803846#post803846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would certainly be an interesting story hook to follow, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Belial's Brood still exists, and were more introspective than outwardly-aggressive like the strix. But it is possible that they are sort of seen with approval by the strix, as they are about losing their Humanity. Whether they're losing their Humanity to become strix or sticking with their original goals would probably be up to you. If you want to go by the books, though, traditionally the Brood serve the Inferno, while the strix are something else. Still, it wouldn't be far-fetched to have the Brood be a sort of birthplace for new stirges.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for your first answered, I'm hesitant about it but it will be an significant element of my Chronicle.<br /> Ok, so about your second statement, do you mean that the Strix are the embodiment of the Beast whatever it takes ? The Brood is scary because it revels in losing one's humanity: it's a path of, shall we say, dark enlightenment. If the Strix had to be a major nemesis I would expect something with more depth than just losing your humanity for the sake of it, I would expect an agenda, a vision. So when I re read the Belial's Brood sourcebook I saw a vision about why it could be important to lose one's humanity and this is what was scarring and amazing about the Brood. To be honest, I'm not sure about the Strix: they look great, they have this air of mystery but ... I'd like to scratch the surface ^^ The Belial's sourcebook did that for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","user":"JPS","date":". 01-08-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:00:26-08:00","id":803903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803814-belial-s-brood-and-the-strix?p=803873#post803873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for your first answered, I'm hesitant about it but it will be an significant element of my Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'd only really come into the spotlight of a sort of Indiana Jones-esque world spanning archaeological game of exploration and adventure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, so about your second statement, do you mean that the Strix are the embodiment of the Beast whatever it takes ? The Brood is scary but it revels in losing one's humanity: it's a path of, shall we say, dark enlightenment. If the Strix had to be a major nemesis I would expect something with more depth than just losing your humanity for the sake of it, I would expect an agenda a vision. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the thing. While the strix do seem to hover around the idea of dragging you away from your Humanity, letting you revel in your Beast, shrugging off the Masquerade, they aren't all like that. They seem as varied as vampires, just in inverse, dark snowflakes. The Brood is very much about, as you said, dark enlightenment. While they're divided on the specifics, it's very specifically their goal. This is one of the reasons why I think the strix aren't really a replacement for the Brood. The Brood are really going to deal with you in an attempt to get you to lower your Humanity, while the strix are more of a generalized antagonist, who can take many roles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So when I re read the Belial's Brood sourcebook I saw a vision about why it could be important to lose one's humanity and this is what was scarring and amazing about the Brood. To be honest, I'm not sure about the Strix: they look great, they have this air of mystery but ... I'd like to scratch the surface ^^ The Belial's sourcebook did that for me. </div> </div> </div>I think the Belial's Brood book was really the best book to have come out in first edition Vampire. Great book. But the strix pose a more varied threat, and not one so easy to deal with as someone who has the same vulnerabilities of almost every other vampire. Their abilities allow them to do all sorts of stuff way beyond the Brood or other vampires. I think we'll see bits and pieces of info about them scattered throughout the line, but yeah, unless we get a full sourcebook you'll probably have to really work on their origins yourself. As a bonus, however, the strix aren't a unified faction, so you can have individual strix with as deep motivations and goals as you want while not being required to have another strix have the same ideas, like the example ones in the core book.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Storyteller's guide will have advice on options for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:37:49-08:00","id":803936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803814-belial-s-brood-and-the-strix?p=803873#post803873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do you mean that the Strix are the embodiment of the Beast whatever it takes ? The Brood is scary because it revels in losing one's humanity: it's a path of, shall we say, dark enlightenment. If the Strix had to be a major nemesis I would expect something with more depth than just losing your humanity for the sake of it, I would expect an agenda, a vision. So when I re read the Belial's Brood sourcebook I saw a vision about why it could be important to lose one's humanity and this is what was scarring and amazing about the Brood. To be honest, I'm not sure about the Strix: they look great, they have this air of mystery but ... I'd like to scratch the surface ^^ The Belial's sourcebook did that for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the Strix are like The Joker. The Joker doesn't have an agenda or a vision, but that doesn't stop him from being a deep and complex villain. At his most basic, he just wants to revel in chaos for its own sake, but there are layers to his character that make him more than just an embodiment of destruction. In my favorite Joker comic, The Killing Joke, he shows that while he doesn't remember exactly how he got the way he is, the one thing he knows for certain is that it was just one bad day that pushed him over the edge. And so, he firmly believes that everyone is just one bad day from becoming just like him.<br /> <br /> The Strix, likewise, believe that every vampire is just one bad day from being just like they are. That's why they delight in dragging vampires' Humanity down; they've got something to prove. They want to show the vampires that deep down, they're all just life-sucking monsters inhabiting corpses, and no matter what rules and moralities they try to impose on themselves, they'll never escape the fact that they're just one bad day from ending up just like the Strix.<br /> <br /> In my view of the Strix, they would find Belial's Brood entertaining. They embrace their Beasts, they cause lots of chaos and destruction, they're just fun guys to be around. But ultimately, they wouldn't like the Brood any more than they like any other vampires. At the end of the day, their ideals about &quot;dark enlightenment&quot; are still just another way to pretend at some moral high ground that makes them more than just Beasts puppeteering human corpses. Their false morality may be more entertaining than the other vampires, but they'll still need to be shown what they really are sooner or later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T13:21:15-08:00","id":803970,"title":